Alli McDermitt
Program 5: Netlog 
CS3411 Spring 2025

As far as I can tell, the program works perfectly — I've tested logging with multiple clients,
and tried to cause every race condition I can think of (log while another client is listing, 
two clients listing, etc.). I would have liked to include some more quality-of-life stuff, namely
some kind of mode indicator beyond the last command, so that one can tell whether or not the
program still has more blocks to list; however, I didn't want to get too far away from the spec
as written, and as exams approach, I need to tell myself not to overthink things more than I must.
Because, to a certain extent, I must.

♥

Addendum for Github: This program creates a TCP server, which accepts a number of messages from
its connected clients, and when a client requests, prints the entire list of messages in blocks
to the requesting client. This allows it to function as a simple network-enabled logger for 
storing data from a series of client connections.

Similarly to Program 4, this program's specification asked for the program to be completed in 9 
steps, which are again included in full, and will be built by the Makefile — however, only 
"logger.c" contains the source needed for full functionality.
